{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-f25223e55e09fabc081e","statement":"\\nonumber\n\\Delta A:=S^T J_n(0)+J_n(0)S\n\n=\n\n\\begin{bmatrix}\n0+s_{21}&s_{11}+s_{22}&s_{21}+s_{23}\n&\\dots& s_{n-1,1}+s_{2n}\n\\\\\n0+s_{31}&s_{12}+s_{32}&s_{22}+s_{33}\n&\\dots& s_{n-1,2}+s_{3n}\n\\\\\n\\hdotsfor{5}\n\\\\\n0+s_{n1}&s_{1,n-1}+s_{n2}&s_{2,n-1}+s_{n3}\n&\\dots& s_{n-1,n-1}+s_{nn}\n\\\\\n0+0&s_{1n}+0&s_{2n}+0 &\\dots&\ns_{n-1,n}+0\n\\end{bmatrix}","source_id":"arXiv:1004.3584","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"50c6901865eee37cda920238caaf7ce99979d8460663c6df16e28e1970ea9227","kind":"equation","label":"Equation 2","ref_key":"ed2","name":"","order":52,"deps":[],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1004.3584","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"da7694bd01118586f2d942a776eec1e2d33ddd2c07a7a628e5c9e0454c9479b3","line":2423,"origin":"latex_env:equation","retrieved_at":"2026-09-29T14:02:49+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v3","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":333,"math_hints":36}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:1004.3584","title":"Miniversal deformations of matrices of bilinear forms","abstract":"V.I. Arnold [Russian Math. Surveys 26 (2) (1971) 29-43] constructed a miniversal deformation of matrices under similarity; that is, a simple normal form to which not only a given square matrix A but all matrices B close to it can be reduced by similarity transformations that smoothly depend on the entries of B. We construct a miniversal deformation of matrices under congruence.","authors":["Andrii R. Dmytryshyn","Vyacheslav Futorny","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2010","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1004.3584","cluster":"representation_theory","macros":{"le":"\\leqslant","ge":"\\geqslant"},"macros_override":["ge","le"]},"deps":[],"dependents":[]}